---
// Figure 1: deployment shape, drawn as plain line art like a LaTeX/TikZ figure.
---
<figure class="fig">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 640 250" role="img" aria-labelledby="f1t">
    <title id="f1t">Clients reach a TLS-terminating Nginx load balancer, which forwards to two Django application servers backed by PostgreSQL, Redis and Celery workers.</title>
    <defs>
      <marker id="ah" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
        <path d="M0 1 L9 5 L0 9" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.2" />
      </marker>
    </defs>

    <g class="edges">
      <path d="M92 45 C130 45 130 125 168 125" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <path d="M92 125 H168" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <path d="M92 205 C130 205 130 125 168 125" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <path d="M268 118 C300 118 300 70 334 70" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <path d="M268 132 C300 132 300 180 334 180" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <path d="M434 70 H500" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <path d="M434 70 C466 70 466 125 500 125" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <path d="M434 180 C466 180 466 125 500 125" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
      <path d="M434 180 H500" marker-end="url(#ah)" />
    </g>

    <g class="nodes">
      <g><rect x="20" y="30" width="72" height="30" /><text x="56" y="50">browser</text></g>
      <g><rect x="20" y="110" width="72" height="30" /><text x="56" y="130">iOS app</text></g>
      <g><rect x="20" y="190" width="72" height="30" /><text x="56" y="210">API client</text></g>

      <g><rect x="168" y="100" width="100" height="50" class="dbl" /><text x="218" y="122">Nginx</text><text x="218" y="140" class="it">TLS, LB</text></g>

      <g><rect x="334" y="48" width="100" height="44" /><text x="384" y="67">Django</text><text x="384" y="84" class="it">app 1</text></g>
      <g><rect x="334" y="158" width="100" height="44" /><text x="384" y="177">Django</text><text x="384" y="194" class="it">app 2</text></g>

      <g><path d="M500 58 v26 a38 7 0 0 0 76 0 v-26 a38 7 0 0 0 -76 0 a38 7 0 0 0 76 0" class="cyl" /><text x="538" y="80">PostgreSQL</text></g>
      <g><rect x="500" y="112" width="76" height="26" /><text x="538" y="130">Redis</text></g>
      <g><rect x="500" y="168" width="76" height="26" /><text x="538" y="186">Celery</text></g>
    </g>

    <text x="56" y="244" class="lab">clients</text>
    <text x="218" y="244" class="lab">edge</text>
    <text x="384" y="244" class="lab">application</text>
    <text x="538" y="244" class="lab">state &amp; jobs</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="caption">
    <b>Fig. 1.</b> The deployment shape shared by most of the systems above: a TLS-terminating
    Nginx load balancer in front of stateless Django application servers, with PostgreSQL for
    state, Redis for caching and queues, and Celery for background work.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .fig { margin: 48px 0 0; padding: 28px 0 0; border-top: 1px solid rgba(34, 31, 27, 0.35); display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 36px; align-items: end; }
  svg { width: 100%; height: auto; color: var(--spot); mix-blend-mode: multiply; filter: url(#ink); }
  .edges path { fill: none; stroke: var(--spot); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .nodes rect, .cyl { fill: rgba(0, 120, 191, 0.07); stroke: var(--spot); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .nodes rect.dbl { stroke-width: 2.2; }
  text { font: 500 13px var(--serif); fill: var(--ink); text-anchor: middle; }
  text.it { font-style: italic; font-size: 12px; fill: var(--ink-2); }
  text.lab { font-size: 12px; font-variant-caps: all-small-caps; letter-spacing: 0.08em; fill: var(--muted); }
  .caption { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--ink-2); border-left: 3px solid var(--spot); padding-left: 16px; }
  .caption b { color: var(--ink); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .fig { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; } }
</style>
